  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The possible values of $x$, which satisfy the trigonometric equation\r\n$\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x-1}{x-2}\\right)+\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{x+2}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "evThz",
      "text": "$\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Lfuaf",
      "text": "$\\pm \\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mGA3S",
      "text": "$\\pm \\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4lpK0",
      "text": "$\\pm 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x-1}{x-2}\\right)+\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{x+2}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\tan ^{-1}\\left[\\frac{\\frac{x-1}{x-2}+\\frac{x+1}{x+2}}{1-\\frac{x-1}{x-2} \\cdot \\frac{x+1}{x+2}}\\right]=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{(x-1)(x+2)+(x-2)(x+1)}{(x-2)(x+2)-(x-1)(x+1)}=\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{x^{2}+x-2+x^{2}-x-2}{x^{2}-4-x^{2}+1}=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ $\\frac{2 x^{2}-4}{-3}=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ $2 x^{2}-4=3$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ $2 x^{2}=1$\r\n$x^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n$x=\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
